course: dictionary
lesson: 4474
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, look at the words and sentences around it. «Harp seal pups are born white on the ice» is about an animal, so here a harp is a kind of seal, not an instrument.
explain: Ask what the sentence is about. «Picture a world music fair: a Ukrainian bandura with dozens of strings... a West African kora that is half harp, half lute» is a list of instruments, so harp here means the musical instrument.
explain: Verbs can have their own meanings too. «Harp on» is informal speech and means to keep talking about the same thing in a boring or annoying way. Try the meaning in the sentence: if it makes sense as nagging, you have found it.
fact: A harp is a large musical instrument with many strings stretched on a tall frame.
fact: You play a harp by plucking the strings with your fingers.
fact: «Harp on» is an informal verb meaning to keep talking about the same thing in a boring or annoying way.
fact: A harmonica is sometimes called a mouth harp or blues harp, but it is a different instrument from a harp.
fact: The harp is a symbol of Ireland and appears on Irish coins.
exercise: «Picture a world music fair: ...a West African kora that is half harp, half lute.» In this sentence, what is a harp? | A small instrument you blow into | *A musical instrument with many strings | A tall tree | A kind of seal that lives on the ice
exercise: «Harp seal pups are born white on the ice.» In this sentence, what is a harp? | *A kind of seal | A harmonica | A large musical instrument | A frame for holding strings
exercise: Dad says, «Stop harping on about your homework.» What does harping on mean here? | Singing a happy song | Losing your way home | *Talking about the same thing again and again in an annoying way | Playing a harp very softly
test: In the Bible, David played the harp to calm King Saul. What is the harp in this story? | A kind of seal | *A large string instrument | A heavy bell | A harmonica
test: «The harmonica is sometimes called a mouth harp.» What is a mouth harp? | A kind of seal | A large string instrument | A bell rung by hand | *A small instrument you play with your mouth
exam: Which sentence uses harp as a verb? | *Please stop harping on about the same old thing | Harp seals live on the ice | The harp sounded sweet in the hall | The harp has a tall frame
